https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IRp856r2moA  (Capo 2) (MC2)

If transposing, play the root chord of the (CaddG) and add the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  The movement from (D) to (CaddG) might be a little uncomfortable at first if you're not use to playing (C) with your pinky on the 1st string.  Keep your pinky on the bottom finger for the rotation to the (G).

TIP:  There's a definite cadence going throughout the song and the (G) (C) (C) sequence after the lines help maintain in.  When you get to the "rockin' in the USA" part you'll come off an (A)  so just either slide your ring finger into the 3rd fret or add your pinky the the 2nd string/3rd fret and strum the |Asus4| once at that point until the following (D).
   

